IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ea-part12-retrenchment`

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), s 96A -- the Employment (Retrenchment
-- Reporting) Notification 2019 (S 200/2019) made under s 96A(1): which
-- employers and which employees it covers (paragraph 2), the duty to report
-- (paragraph 3), the time (paragraph 4), the form (paragraph 5) and the
-- particulars (the Schedule); and how it fills the supplied facts that
-- ea-part12-retrenchment.l4 left open.
--
-- Edition: S 200/2019, informal consolidation (version in force from
-- 1 November 2021, as amended by S 781/2021), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/EmA1968-S200-2019.txt. Paragraph numbers were
-- taken from the body of the deposit and agree with its arrangement table.
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0289 (Haziq scenario, event from the
-- Haziq scenario, event h065): an employer with 40 employees retrenches 12 of
-- them in one exercise -- must it notify the Commissioner, within what time,
-- and with what particulars? ea-part12-retrenchment.l4 showed that s 96A
-- leaves every one of those to a Gazette notification; this module encodes the
-- notification.
--
-- DAYS ARE DAY NUMBERS. Day 0 is Monday 1 November 2021, the day from which
-- the current paragraph 3 reaches a notice of retrenchment. Day n is n days
-- later, so (n MODULO 7) is 0 on a Monday, 5 on a Saturday and 6 on a Sunday.
-- Which days are public holidays is NOT in the deposit: the caller supplies
-- them as a list of day numbers.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the version of the Notification in force from 1 April 2019 to
-- 31 October 2021 (not deposited; the deposit shows one definition "Deleted by
-- S 781/2021" without its old words); what the form at the Ministry of
-- Manpower website contains; the Public Holidays Act and any list of public
-- holidays; the Interpretation Act 1965 on the computation of time (not
-- retrieved); whether one report may cover several notices given on different
-- days (Schedule para 1(f) speaks of "the number of retrenched employees who
-- are the subject of the retrenchment report", which suggests a report can
-- cover more than one, but the deposit does not say how notices are grouped);
-- the content (as opposed to the presence) of each particular; retrenchment
-- benefit itself.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules
-- approach. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human
-- gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Employment (Retrenchment Reporting) Notification 2019`

§§ `Paragraph 2(2) -- which employees the Notification speaks of`

-- Para 2(2): "any reference to an employee is a reference to an employee who
-- has or works under a contract of service (whenever made) -- (a) that does
-- not specify an end date for the contract; or (b) that has a term of
-- employment of at least 6 months."
--
-- The person must also be an "employee" under s 2(1) of the Act (no seafarer,
-- no domestic worker): the Notification is made under s 96A, which speaks of
-- "the retrenchment of any employee". That test is in ea-part12-retrenchment.l4
-- and is taken here as a supplied fact.
DECLARE `Contract of service` HAS
    `specifies an end date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `term of employment in months` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the contract` IS A `Contract of service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract brings the employee within the Notification` IF
        (NOT `the contract`'s `specifies an end date`)
    OR  `the contract`'s `term of employment in months` AT LEAST 6

§§ `Paragraph 2(1), 2(3) -- which employers`

-- Para 2(1): "'employer' means an employer with 10 or more employees".
-- Para 2(3): "Whether or not an employer has 10 or more employees is to be
-- worked out as at the time when a notice of retrenchment is given by the
-- employer to an employee who becomes retrenched, regardless when the notice
-- takes effect."
-- Reading: because of para 2(2), only employees on open-ended contracts or
-- terms of at least 6 months count towards the 10. So the number supplied is
-- of THOSE employees, on the day the notice is given.
`the smallest workforce the Notification reaches` MEANS 10

GIVEN `employees within the Notification on the day notice is given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an employer within the Notification` IF
    `employees within the Notification on the day notice is given` AT LEAST `the smallest workforce the Notification reaches`

§§ `Paragraph 2(1) -- what "retrench" means`

-- Para 2(1): "'retrench', in relation to an employee, means to terminate the
-- employee's contract of service AT THE INITIATIVE OF THE EMPLOYER because of
-- REDUNDANCY or ANY REORGANISATION of the employer's profession, business,
-- trade or work".
GIVEN `the employer initiated the termination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reason is redundancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reason is a reorganisation of the employer's business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a retrenchment within the Notification` IF
        `the employer initiated the termination`
    AND (`the reason is redundancy` OR `the reason is a reorganisation of the employer's business`)

§§ `Paragraph 3 -- the duty to report`

-- Para 3(1): "Every employer must give to the Commissioner a retrenchment
-- report in accordance with sub-paragraph (2) if, ON OR AFTER 1 NOVEMBER 2021,
-- the employer gives ANY of its employees a notice of his or her retrenchment,
-- REGARDLESS WHEN THE NOTICE TAKES EFFECT OR WHEN THE EMPLOYMENT ENDS."
--
-- There is no minimum number retrenched and no period over which notices are
-- added up: one notice to one covered employee is enough. The day the notice
-- takes effect is carried only to show that nothing turns on it.
`the first day paragraph 3 reaches` MEANS 0

DECLARE `Notice of retrenchment` HAS
    `the person is an employee under section 2(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract` IS A `Contract of service`
    `employees within the Notification on the day notice is given` IS A NUMBER
    `the employer initiated the termination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the reason is redundancy or a reorganisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the notice is given` IS A NUMBER
    `the day the notice takes effect` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the notice` IS A `Notice of retrenchment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a retrenchment report must be given for the notice` IF
        `the notice`'s `the person is an employee under section 2(1) of the Act`
    AND `the contract brings the employee within the Notification` (`the notice`'s `the contract`)
    AND `is an employer within the Notification` (`the notice`'s `employees within the Notification on the day notice is given`)
    AND `is a retrenchment within the Notification` (`the notice`'s `the employer initiated the termination`) (`the notice`'s `the reason is redundancy or a reorganisation`) FALSE
    AND `the notice`'s `the day the notice is given` AT LEAST `the first day paragraph 3 reaches`

§§ `Paragraph 4 -- the time`

-- Para 4: "Every retrenchment report must be given to the Commissioner NOT
-- LATER THAN 5 WORKING DAYS AFTER THE DAY that the employer gives the notice of
-- retrenchment". Para 2(1): "'working day' means a day other than a Saturday,
-- Sunday or public holiday."
-- Reading: the count starts on the day after the notice is given, and the
-- report is in time if given on or before the 5th working day so counted.
`the number of working days allowed` MEANS 5

GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekday of day` `the day` MEANS ((`the day` MODULO 7) PLUS 7) MODULO 7

GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER, `the days` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the day` `is among` `the days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the days`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN d FOLLOWED BY rest THEN (d EQUALS `the day`) OR (`the day` `is among` rest)

GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER, `public holidays` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a working day` IF
        `the weekday of day` `the day` LESS THAN 5
    AND (NOT (`the day` `is among` `public holidays`))

-- The day on which a count of `still to count` working days, beginning after
-- `counted up to`, ends.
GIVEN `counted up to` IS A NUMBER, `still to count` IS A NUMBER, `public holidays` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the working-day count ends on` `counted up to` `still to count` `public holidays` MEANS
    IF `still to count` AT MOST 0
    THEN `counted up to`
    ELSE IF `is a working day` (`counted up to` PLUS 1) `public holidays`
         THEN `the working-day count ends on` (`counted up to` PLUS 1) (`still to count` MINUS 1) `public holidays`
         ELSE `the working-day count ends on` (`counted up to` PLUS 1) `still to count` `public holidays`

GIVEN `the day the notice is given` IS A NUMBER, `public holidays` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day for the retrenchment report` `the day the notice is given` `public holidays` MEANS
    `the working-day count ends on` `the day the notice is given` `the number of working days allowed` `public holidays`

GIVEN `the day the notice is given` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the report is given` IS A NUMBER
      `public holidays` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the report is given in time` IF
    `the day the report is given` AT MOST `the last day for the retrenchment report` `the day the notice is given` `public holidays`

§§ `Paragraph 5 -- the form`

-- Para 5: "Every retrenchment report must be in the form provided at the
-- website of the Ministry of Manpower at http://www.mom.gov.sg, UNLESS THE
-- COMMISSIONER ALLOWS OTHERWISE IN ANY PARTICULAR CASE."
GIVEN `the report uses the form at the Ministry of Manpower website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner allowed otherwise in this case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the report is in the required form` IF
        `the report uses the form at the Ministry of Manpower website`
    OR  `the Commissioner allowed otherwise in this case`

§§ `The Schedule -- the particulars`

-- Para 3(2): "The retrenchment report by the employer must contain ALL the
-- information specified in the Schedule in relation to the employee who is
-- given a notice of retrenchment by the employer."
-- Schedule para 1: details of the employer, "including the following":
--   (a) name and address; (b) "the employer's trade name IF DIFFERENT"; (c) the
--   nature of the business; (d) "the name of any trade union ... recognised by
--   the employer ..., and whether that trade union was consulted"; (e) the
--   contact person; (f) "the number of retrenched employees who are the subject
--   of the retrenchment report"; (g) "the number of employees of the employer on
--   the date the notice of retrenchment is given, including a breakdown of the
--   number of citizens of Singapore, ... permanent residents ... and ...
--   foreigners".
-- Schedule para 2: details of each retrenched employee, "including":
--   (a) name and identity card or foreign identification number; (b) job title
--   immediately before the notice; (c) citizen, permanent resident or
--   foreigner; (d) the date the notice is given; (e) the effective date; (f) the
--   retrenchment benefits paid or to be paid; (g) "IF NO RETRENCHMENT BENEFITS
--   WERE PAID ..., the reasons for not paying so"; (h) the employment
--   facilitation assistance provided or to be provided.
-- "Including" means the lists are not closed on their face; this encoding
-- lists only what the Schedule names.
DECLARE `Schedule particular` IS ONE OF
    `the employer's name and address`
    `the employer's trade name`
    `the nature of the employer's business`
    `the recognised trade union and whether it was consulted`
    `the employer's contact person`
    `the number of retrenched employees in the report`
    `the employer's workforce on the notice date by citizenship`
    `the employee's name and identification number`
    `the employee's job title before the notice`
    `the employee's citizenship or residence status`
    `the date the notice was given`
    `the effective date of retrenchment`
    `the retrenchment benefits paid or to be paid`
    `the reasons no retrenchment benefits were paid`
    `the employment facilitation assistance`

DECLARE `Schedule circumstances` HAS
    `the trade name differs from the name` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer recognises a trade union` IS A BOOLEAN
    `retrenchment benefits were paid to the employee` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Reading of 1(d): where no union is recognised there is no name to give.
GIVEN `the particular` IS A `Schedule particular`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Schedule circumstances`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the particular is required` IS
    CONSIDER `the particular`
    WHEN `the employer's trade name` THEN `the circumstances`'s `the trade name differs from the name`
    WHEN `the recognised trade union and whether it was consulted` THEN `the circumstances`'s `the employer recognises a trade union`
    WHEN `the reasons no retrenchment benefits were paid` THEN NOT `the circumstances`'s `retrenchment benefits were paid to the employee`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the particular` IS A `Schedule particular`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the particular is about the employer` IF
        `the particular` EQUALS `the employer's name and address`
    OR  `the particular` EQUALS `the employer's trade name`
    OR  `the particular` EQUALS `the nature of the employer's business`
    OR  `the particular` EQUALS `the recognised trade union and whether it was consulted`
    OR  `the particular` EQUALS `the employer's contact person`
    OR  `the particular` EQUALS `the number of retrenched employees in the report`
    OR  `the particular` EQUALS `the employer's workforce on the notice date by citizenship`

-- Schedule para 1: (a), (c), (e), (f), (g) always; (b) and (d) when they apply.
GIVEN `the circumstances` IS A `Schedule circumstances`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of employer particulars required` `the circumstances` MEANS
    5
    PLUS (IF `the circumstances`'s `the trade name differs from the name` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF `the circumstances`'s `the employer recognises a trade union` THEN 1 ELSE 0)

-- Schedule para 2: (a) to (f) and (h) always; (g) only where no benefits were paid.
GIVEN `the circumstances` IS A `Schedule circumstances`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of particulars required for each retrenched employee` `the circumstances` MEANS
    IF `the circumstances`'s `retrenchment benefits were paid to the employee` THEN 7 ELSE 8

§§ `Section 96A(2) -- the Notification as the facts ea-part12-retrenchment.l4 left open`

-- The Notification was made "in exercise of the powers conferred by section
-- 96A(1)" and the deposit records it as the current version as at 13 October
-- 2026, so "a notification is in force" is TRUE. It applies to the employer if
-- it has 10 or more covered employees; it requires information on the
-- retrenchment if at least one notice of retrenchment to a covered employee was
-- given on or after 1 November 2021.
GIVEN `covered employees on the day notice is given` IS A NUMBER
      `notices needing a report` IS A NUMBER
      `notices reported in time, in form and with every particular` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A RetrenchmentFacts
`the section 96A facts under the 2019 Notification` `covered employees on the day notice is given` `notices needing a report` `notices reported in time, in form and with every particular` MEANS
    RetrenchmentFacts WITH
        `a notification under section 96A(1) is in force` IS TRUE
        `the notification applies to the employer or to a class the employer is in` IS `is an employer within the Notification` `covered employees on the day notice is given`
        `the notification requires information on this retrenchment` IS `notices needing a report` GREATER THAN 0
        `number of employees the employer has` IS `covered employees on the day notice is given`
        `number of employees retrenched` IS `notices needing a report`
        `number of retrenched employees for whom every requirement was met` IS `notices reported in time, in form and with every particular`
